{
  "summary": "Adds CreateMultisigDescriptor() to script/descriptor to construct and validate ranged multipath multisig descriptors from cosigner keys. The function supports P2WSH (wsh(sortedmulti(...))) and P2TR (tr(NUMS, sortedmulti_a(...))) output types and appends descriptor checksums. It enforces validation rules including threshold range, duplicate key detection, rejection of private keys, and requirement of key origin information on bare account xpubs.",
  "problem": "Setting up multisig wallets requires callers to hand-craft descriptor strings manually, which often leads to string interpolation without validation for key expressions, duplicate cosigners, derivation paths, or valid thresholds.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The multisig setup flows need to assemble a descriptor from collected cosigner keys without hand-crafting the descriptor string, which today means bash interpolation with no validation of key forms, duplicates, or threshold.'",
    "Author references tracking issue #35645 ('Multisig Wizard tracking issue') for the intended consumer."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#35645"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Commit e0b664f141 adds P2TR support using a hardcoded unspendable xpub as the internal key to accommodate hardware signers, which the commit note acknowledges introduces potential wallet fingerprinting.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Adds CreateMultisigDescriptor() to construct and validate ranged multipath multisig descriptors with checksums for P2WSH and P2TR. Today, multisig setup flows lack a dedicated constructor and rely on ad-hoc string formatting without validation of key formats, duplicate cosigners, derivation paths, or threshold bounds. The author notes this helper is needed so setup flows avoid bash interpolation without validation, supporting the multisig wizard backend tracked in issue #35645.",
